[h2]0.8.3[/h2]
[h3]Every building is smaller now[/h3]
The second shrink is finished: Deep Frontier's buildings now sit close to vanilla Iron Teeth scale. Only the Nuclear Reactor and the "Plant" buildings (power, water treatment, electrolysis, cryogenic and uranium plants) keep their size. Recipes, workers and power use are unchanged.
[list]
[*][b]Mines fit their deposits:[/b] the Deep Mine and the Sandstone and Limestone Quarries are 5x5 and cover their vein or seam exactly. The Deep Drill is 4x4.
[*][b]Civic:[/b] Restaurant 6x5 (all 14 seats kept), Fish Hatchery 5x5, Materials Laboratory 5x4, Town Plaza 5x5, Technical School 4x3, Public Health Lab 4x3, Greenhouse 6x3, Observation Deck 3x3.
[*][b]Industry:[/b] Deep Ore Processor 5x4, Precision Machine Works 5x4, Food Packaging Works 4x3, Chemical Works 4x3, Archive Excavation 4x4.
[*][b]Late game:[/b] Launch Pad 7x7, Radioactive Waste Export 4x3, Reinforced Hydro Turbine 4x6 (same water flow and power).
[*]Build costs are what they were before the shrink.
[/list]
[b]Existing saves:[/b] shrunk buildings keep their place. Deep Mines and quarries move onto their vein or seam, mirrored buildings stay on the same ground, and a path on ground the old building left free is removed instead of the building. Things that stood on a roof or deck the smaller building no longer has are removed, as the loading notice lists. Re-lay paths to moved doors and reconnect pipes on moved inlets.

[h3]Clearer progression[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Every build menu reads left to right in unlock order[/b], including where Deep Frontier buildings sit among the base game's.
[*][b]Later buildings cost more science.[/b] Early unlocks are unchanged; steel, chemistry, machinery and coal power now unlock at 9,000-20,000, the frontier at 25,000-75,000, the launch program at 75,000-200,000, the nuclear chain at 300,000-600,000, and the [b]Nuclear Reactor stays the last unlock[/b] at 1,000,000.
[*]The Materials Laboratory stays at 12,000 as the fast route to more science. Rocket missions now pay 250,000 and 500,000 science.
[*]Tide cleanup comes sooner: the Radioactive Water Recovery Pump and Outfall unlock at 50,000. The Grocery Store unlocks at 3,000. Concrete platforms cost 500 science per tile again.
[*]The Reactor Charging Bay moved to Nuclear fuel and the Radioactive Waste Vault to Radioactive waste.
[*]Power draw follows the new unlocks, so mid-game buildings draw more power.
[/list]

[h3]Maps[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Diorama, Cliffside and Beaverome can now finish the game[/b], with sites for the quarries, the plants and the Nuclear Reactor.
[*]No more "this map is short of" notice at the start of a new game.
[/list]

[h3]Fixes and clearer texts[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]The Restaurant kitchen takes turns between dishes again[/b]; with several cooks it could get stuck cooking one dish.
[*]Pipe hints now name the valve modes you see ("Fill" and "Extract"). Several wrong tooltips are fixed, every building has its own flavor line, and names follow the base game's style.
[/list]
